When the task message names the files to deliver, present exactly those — no others and none missing. Otherwise the deliverables are the files in this execution's outputs/ folder (the task workspace), which the calling system reads as the task's result. Never present helper scripts or intermediate data from .work/, and never a file that is not final. Call it once, after the files are final, listing every deliverable; each one gets a download and preview card. Paths must be inside the project directory — save or copy a deliverable there first if it was written elsewhere. Presenting the same path again later records a new version.
